  {
    "event_num": 55,
    "timestamp": "2026-08-19T15:32:30.122814+00:00",
    "author": "coordinator",
    "type": "final_response",
    "text": "### \ud83d\udea8 EMERGENCY NOTICE\n**If this is a life-threatening emergency, please call 911 immediately.**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Incident Classification\n* **Incident ID:** FIRE-2026-153126\n* **Incident Type:** Fire (Smoke Reported)\n* **Severity:** Low (as classified by automated triage, though actively being monitored due to reports of occupants inside)\n* **Location:** Floor 2, Room 215 - Science Lab (Zone: **West Wing Floor 2 / west-wing-f2**)\n* **Active Playbook:** `playbook-fire-v1` (Pre-approved Fire Playbook)\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Safety & Resource Intelligence\n\n#### **Evacuation Routes & Assembly Points**\n* **Primary Evacuation Route:** West hallway Floor 2 \u27a1\ufe0f West Stairwell \u27a1\ufe0f Door 1 (West Exit) leading to the staff parking lot.\n* **Wheelchair-Accessible Route:** West hallway Floor 2 \u27a1\ufe0f Elevator (mid-hall) \u27a1\ufe0f Floor 1 \u27a1\ufe0f West corridor \u27a1\ufe0f Door 1.\n  * *Crucial Accessibility Note:* The elevator requires a key (located in the Main Office, or alternatively in **Room 201** as noted in historical lessons).\n* **Primary Assembly Point:** **Athletic Field (Primary)** \u2013 Behind the gym past the track (500ft from the building).\n* **Alternate Assembly Point:** **Staff Parking Lot (Alternate)** \u2013 West side staff parking lot near Oak Street.\n* **Off-Site Reunification:** **First Baptist Church** \u2013 1300 Oak Street (across the street).\n\n#### **Emergency Resources Near Incident (West-Wing-F2)**\n* \ud83d\udd25 **Fire Extinguisher:** Located in the **West hallway F2 near Room 215 (Science Lab)**.\n* \ud83e\ude79 **First Aid Kits:** Located in the **Library front desk** (Floor 2, bottom drawer). Nearby first aid kits on Floor 1 are in the Nurse's Office (Room 108) and the Main Office behind the reception counter.\n* \u2764\ufe0f **AEDs:** Located on Floor 1: **Hallway B outside Room 112** (West-Wing-F1), Main Office lobby, and the Gym entrance.\n* \ud83c\udf92 **Trauma Kit:** Located in the **Security Office** inside the admin area (Floor 1, locked cabinet).\n* \ud83d\udcde **Emergency Phones:** Main Office front desk (direct line to 911) and Gym office (Coach Williams' desk phone).\n\n#### **Nearby Emergency Services**\n* **Fire Station:** Nashville Fire Station 9 (0.8 miles | ~3 mins ETA) \u2014 *Phone: 615-862-5421*\n* **Police Station:** Metro Nashville Police - Central Precinct (1.5 miles | ~4 mins ETA) \u2014 *Phone: 615-862-8600*\n* **Hospitals:** \n  * TriStar Centennial Medical Center (1.8 miles | ~5 mins ETA | Level II Trauma)\n  * Vanderbilt Children's Hospital (3.4 miles | ~9 mins ETA | Level I Pediatric Trauma)\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udc65 Accountability & Personnel Status\nA facility-wide check-in request has been sent out to all **34** registered personnel at the Jefferson facility. Because the incident is active and has just begun, all personnel are currently categorized as unaccounted for (silent/unknown) pending their check-ins.\n\n#### **High-Priority Escalation (Mobility Limitations)**\nTwo individuals with mobility needs are on the roster. **Emergency response and Floor Wardens should prioritize searching and evacuating these locations:**\n1. **Mrs. Thompson (p021)** \u2013 Room 204 (Floor 2, near the incident zone). *Requires elevator evacuation.*\n2. **Mrs. Davis (p008)** \u2013 Room 104 (Floor 1).\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\udde0 Prior Lessons & Historical Insights\nBased on previous fire drills at the Jefferson facility, response teams must observe the following:\n\n1. **Science Lab Gas Shutoff:** The Floor Warden (Ms. Johnson, West Wing F2) must verify that the **gas shutoff valve located on the east wall of Room 215 (Science Lab)** is fully closed before reporting Floor 2 West as clear.\n2. **Elevator Key Staging:** Retrieving the elevator key from the Floor 1 main office can delay mobility evacuations. **A duplicate elevator key is pre-staged in Room 201** (Mrs. Nguyen\u2019s classroom, Floor Warden East F2) for immediate Floor 2 access to assist Mrs. Thompson.\n3. **Stairwell Bottleneck Prevention:** Simultaneous evacuation of Room 215 (Science Lab) and Room 210 can clog the west stairwell. It is recommended to **stagger evacuations by exiting Room 215 approximately 30 seconds before Room 210** to ensure a smooth flow down the stairs."
  }
